lilt data files: provenance and licences

gold.tsv, silver.tsv
  misaki 0.9.4 data/us_gold.json and data/us_silver.json (hexgrad), after
  misaki's own grow_dictionary(), re-serialised as sorted TSV by
  scripts/lilt_golden.py. misaki is distributed under the Apache License 2.0
  (Copyright hexgrad); the dictionaries ship inside that package with no
  separate licence. Upstream does not document their derivation.

tok_rules.tsv
  spaCy 3.8 English tokenizer special cases (explosion/spaCy, MIT licence,
  Copyright (C) 2016-2024 ExplosionAI GmbH, 2016 spaCy GmbH, 2015 Matthew
  Honnibal), exported by scripts/lilt_golden.py.

tagger.bin
  Averaged-perceptron weights trained by `ribt lilt train-tagger` on
  spaCy en_core_web_sm 3.8 (MIT) predictions over corpus.txt. No treebank
  data was used.

corpus.txt, golden_eval.tsv
  Sentences from WordNet 3.0 glosses/examples (Princeton University, WordNet
  3.0 licence: free use with copyright notice, "WordNet 3.0 Copyright 2006 by
  Princeton University. All rights reserved."), and hand-written edge cases; goldens are misaki 0.9.4 output on them.
